      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "An improved synthesis of a phosphopeptidomimetic prodrug targeting the Src Homology 2 (SH2) domain of signal transducer and activator of transcription 6 (STAT6) is reported. In our convergent methodology, we employed a phosphotyrosine surrogate active ester harboring pivaloyloxymethyl groups, which efficiently coupled to tert-butylglycinyl proline diarylamide. Biological evaluation of 1 has not been reported. We show that it inhibits STAT6 phosphorylation in intact human bronchial epithelial cells, suggesting potential application in the treatment of asthma."},
